From: ThinkSmart LineageOS 24 project (tsv-dev)
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a5xx: disable ring preemption on A506

Under a 4 h TsvBench soak (120 rounds, Night Light toggled every round)
the A506 hit "CP | opcode error | possible opcode=0x00000000" followed by
"hangcheck detected gpu lockup rb 2" (recovered by the kernel).
Mesa puts normal contexts on ring 2 (prio 6 of 12) and SurfaceFlinger's
high-priority RenderEngine context on ring 0, so the GPU preempts on
nearly every composition. All four 2024 a5xx preemption fixes are
already in this tree. Run the A506 on one ring, like the A510.

Same 4 h soak with this patch: 0 lockups (was 1), and with Night Light on
(all frames GPU-composited) missed vsyncs per 15 s scene dropped from
18.6-21.7 to 0.3-1.2 in list/anim/canvas. No scene got worse.


--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
@@ -1746,7 +1746,12 @@
 
 	nr_rings = 4;
 
-	if (config->info->revn == 510)
+	/*
+	 * A506 (msm8953) locks up with a CP opcode error after ring
+	 * preemption under sustained load, even with the 2024 preemption
+	 * fixes. Run it with a single ring like the A510.
+	 */
+	if (config->info->revn == 510 || config->info->revn == 506)
 		nr_rings = 1;
 
 	ret = adreno_gpu_init(dev, pdev, adreno_gpu, config->info->funcs, nr_rings);
